  "narrative": {
    "intro": "M C Dean obligated $401M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. M C Dean won 572 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $701K, and obligations are down 4.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $267M, followed by the Department of Transportation with $53.6M and the Department of Justice with $35.9M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest NAICS market for M C Dean, with obligations of $161M, followed by Engineering Services at $94.1M and Security Systems Services at $82.4M. Historical obligations show variability: FY21 was $355M, FY22 was $323M, FY23 was $301M, FY24 was $308M, and FY25 was $418M. The FY2026 to date total of $401M remains below FY25 but above several prior years. Contract activity spans telecommunications, engineering, security systems, and systems design, reflecting a mix of services and electrical work across civilian and defense agencies.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are M C Dean's biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is M C Dean's largest federal customer, with $267M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Civilian buyers include the Department of Transportation with $53.6M and the Department of Justice with $35.9M. The General Services Administration obligated $29.6M and several smaller agencies each account for single-digit millions or less."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What work does M C Dean sell to the government?",
        "body": "Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest market for M C Dean at $161M in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $94.1M and Security Systems Services at $82.4M. M C Dean also performs Computer Systems Design Services, Facilities Support Services, electrical contracting, and manufacturing-related work across multiple smaller NAICS categories. This mix indicates a portfolio of telecommunications, engineering, security, and electrical services."
      }
    ]
